+# LangGraph Executor (Aegis)
+
+Overview
+- This component provides a durable executor for graph-style plans (LangGraph-style). It offers:
+  - plan persistence (SQLite)
+  - topology-aware execution (Kahn's algorithm)
+  - per-node safety enforcement via ops.agent.orchestrator.run_action (which invokes safety_monitor)
+  - REST API for submission / status (FastAPI)
+
+How to run (dev)
+1. Install requirements:
+   pip install -r ops/langgraph/requirements.txt
+2. Start the server:
+   python3 ops/langgraph/server.py
+3. Submit a demo plan:
+   python3 planners/langgraph_client_stub.py
+4. Poll status:
+   curl http://localhost:8088/status/demo-plan-1
+
+Notes & next steps
+- This is a self-contained executor. To integrate with a specific LangGraph planner, either:
+  - Replace planners/langgraph_client_stub.py with a client that pulls plans from your planner and POSTs to /submit, or
+  - Implement a planner-adapter plugin that calls manager.submit_plan(...) directly.
+- For production: replace SQLite with a durable DB (Postgres), add authentication, TLS for the REST endpoint, and a supervisor (systemd/k8s) to manage the process.
+
