+# LangGraph Integration Overview
+
+This patch introduces a durable LangGraph executor service that can accept graph plans and execute them safely inside Aegis.
+
+Key components:
+- ops/langgraph/server.py — REST API (FastAPI) to submit and monitor plans.
+- ops/langgraph/executor.py — execution engine with topological ordering and concurrency.
+- ops/langgraph/persistence.py — SQLite persistence for plans and node results.
+- planners/langgraph_client_stub.py — example adapter that submits plans to the executor.
+- services/agents/langgraph_end_to_end_demo.py — end-to-end demo script.
+
+Integration notes:
+- The executor calls ops.agent.orchestrator.run_action for node execution — this ensures safety checks (OPA + safety_monitor) and evidence manifests are generated per action.
+- For production, replace SQLite with Postgres, add authentication (OIDC) and TLS on the REST server, and run the server behind an ingress/Service.
